+		 * is exactly the instruction about to execute. On a hit we set the hit
+		 * flag and break out of S9xMainLoop, leaving PBPC untouched on the
+		 * un-executed instruction: the CPU is frozen precisely at the
+		 * breakpoint. The host polls romdev_pcbreak_get after retro_run, reads
